    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. The existing code already derives `membershipTier` from stored fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`) via `Owner.getMembershipTier()`, and builds shared households via `joinHousehold()` in `OwnerRestControllerV1`. I followed that same pattern:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with accessors, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, falling through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules otherwise.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.joinHousehold()`** \u2014 when an owner joins a household, it now stamps the household's member count (existing members + the new owner) onto the new owner *and* every existing member (re-saving them), so the shared size reads back from any member.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_size` column so the field persists across all profiles (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nFor the test scenario: the 1st and 2nd members get household sizes 1 and 2 (not GOLD); creating the 3rd member sets the household size to 3 on all three, so the third owner reads back as `GOLD`.\n\nThis is a non-git repo, so no commit was made.",
